exports[`every page > /projects/university-projects/otams renders 1`] = `"<main class="terminal"><article class="page"><header class="page-header"><h1 class="accent bold">~/projects/university-projects/otams</h1><div class="muted" aria-hidden="true">------------------------------------</div></header><p class="bold">OTAMS: Online Tutoring Appointment Management System</p><section class="section"><h2 class="section-heading">Overview</h2><p>A team-built Android app (Group 7, SEG2105) that gives students, tutors and administrators one platform for tutoring sessions. Built over four deliverables with a team of four.</p><p>Year: 2025</p></section><section class="section"><h2 class="section-heading">Problem being solved</h2><p>Tutoring sessions were hard to manage: students need to find and book tutors, tutors need to publish availability, and someone has to vet who joins.</p></section><section class="section"><h2 class="section-heading">Main features</h2><ul class="bullets"><li>Students search tutors by course, book sessions, cancel up to 24 hours before, and rate tutors</li><li>Tutors create availability in 30-minute slots with overlap prevention, and manage their sessions</li><li>Administrators approve or reject registrations from an inbox; login is gated on approval status</li><li>Role-based registration and login for students, tutors and administrators</li></ul></section><section class="section"><h2 class="section-heading">Technologies used</h2><ul class="bullets"><li>Java</li><li>Android</li><li>Firebase Authentication</li><li>Cloud Firestore</li><li>RecyclerView</li><li>Espresso</li></ul></section><section class="section"><h2 class="section-heading">Architecture and implementation</h2><ul class="bullets"><li>Activity-based navigation with RecyclerView lists and custom adapters</li><li>Backend layer of use cases (login, logout, register student/tutor) behind an AuthService and an AuthRepository interface</li><li>Firestore holds users, approval status, availability and sessions</li></ul></section><section class="section"><h2 class="section-heading">My contributions</h2><ul class="bullets"><li>Backend infrastructure: account creation logic, Firestore schema design and the user status model</li><li>Administrator backend: approval workflow, status gating at login and Firestore query optimization</li><li>Merged the final deliverable and submitted the final report</li></ul></section><section class="section"><h2 class="section-heading">Challenges</h2><ul class="bullets"><li>Merge conflicts on a shared main branch, once wiping the codebase; fixed with feature branches, pull-before-push and pull request reviews</li><li>Firebase setup issues (misplaced google-services.json, permissive security rules hiding bugs); fixed by documenting setup and tightening rules feature by feature</li><li>Navigation running before Firestore queries finished; fixed with proper callbacks and loading states</li><li>Time-slot overlap checks flagging adjacent slots; fixed by storing times as epoch milliseconds with clear boundary rules</li></ul></section><section class="section"><h2 class="section-heading">Technical specifications</h2><ul class="bullets"><li>Platform: Android, written in Java 11</li><li>Build: Gradle (Kotlin DSL), minSdk 24, targetSdk 36, Google Services plugin</li><li>Backend: Firebase Authentication and Cloud Firestore</li><li>UI: AndroidX AppCompat, Material, ConstraintLayout, RecyclerView</li><li>Tests: JUnit and Espresso</li></ul></section><section class="section"><h2 class="section-heading">Links</h2><dl class="fields"><div class="field-row"><dt class="muted">repository</dt><dd>Not public</dd></div><div class="field-row"><dt class="muted">live demo</dt><dd>None</dd></div></dl></section><section class="section"><h2 class="section-heading">Related</h2><ul class="bullets"><li><a href="/courses/SEG2105" data-discover="true">SEG2105 course</a></li></ul></section></article><div class="line input-line"><span class="prompt"><span class="prompt-user">rayyan@portfolio</span>:<span class="prompt-path">~/projects/university-projects/otams</span>$ </span><span class="input-mirror" aria-hidden="true"><span class="cursor"> </span></span><input class="input-native" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" autocorrect="off" autocapitalize="off" enterkeyhint="go" aria-label="Terminal command input" type="text" value=""></div></main>"`;

